{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530784-v20-dav20-and-earlier-additional-protean-4-shapes","id":1530784,"title":"[V20/DAV20 and earlier] Additional Protean 4 shapes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-13T23:13:12-08:00","id":1530784,"title":"[V20/DAV20 and earlier] Additional Protean 4 shapes","content":"Hi has there ever been in any of the older editions an option that would allow to learn additinal animal shapes for Protean 4?<br /> <br /> I know that there is the Totemic Change Merit, but I mean something you get after character creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T04:40:55-08:00","id":1530800,"title":"","content":"I think one could do it with combined disciplines, but it would not be just a different animal, but likely appropriate improvements depending on the disciplines involved, ex: bear form with Potence (was there something along these lines in the manual for Nordic vampires?); stealthy animal form with Obfuscate; maybe a large feline with Celerity; etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T05:37:48-08:00","id":1530891,"title":"","content":"I do recall it being written and mentioned that there are tales of Gangrel Vampires taking form of &quot;noble beasts of prey&quot; when using the Protean Discipline. That is, of a doe or a stag. There is also an ability ( either Protean or Protean and Animalism ) that allows hiding in, resting, and travelling with an animal. Also I think that Toreador Kindred should have a Protean form of a swan bird available.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-18T18:07:27-08:00","id":1531078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530784-v20-dav20-and-earlier-additional-protean-4-shapes?p=1530891#post1530891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do recall it being written and mentioned that there are tales of Gangrel Vampires taking form of &quot;noble beasts of prey&quot; when using the Protean Discipline. That is, of a doe or a stag. There is also an ability ( either Protean or Protean and Animalism ) that allows hiding in, resting, and travelling with an animal. Also I think that Toreador Kindred should have a Protean form of a swan bird available.</div> </div> </div> </div>I most clearly remember that content being from one of the two Gangrel clanbooks (which edition's is anyone's guess), as well as Libellus Sanguinis 3. The &quot;noble beast of prey&quot; part referred to alternate flight forms, as the fight form was typically an apex predator indigenous to (and most associated with) the region the Gangrel either lived as a mortal, or spent their first winters.<br /> <br /> But, that was Gangrel-only with the sole exception of the Tlacique, whose fight form was typically that of a jaguar, not a wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 02-18-2024, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T01:07:24-08:00","id":1531096,"title":"","content":"Saw recently that VDA20 has any user of Protean take forms linked to the <i>mythology</i> (I think vampire mythology) of their area. Which is funny because blood-drinkers in Greek mythology are usually snake-themed, while I recall Arab stories of seducing blood-drinkers with legs like goats. The bat-and-wolf vampire legends may be more typical of Eastern and Central Europe, where at first there was not much of a distinction between vampires and werewolves in folklore. <br /> I guess STs can have some fun sorting that out.<br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T06:25:08-08:00","id":1531109,"title":"","content":"Considering that there were a few places where vampires could shape change into cows was part of the mythology, I am now visualizing an undead blood drinking bovine on a rampage and still failing to intimidate anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T08:57:05-08:00","id":1531124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530784-v20-dav20-and-earlier-additional-protean-4-shapes?p=1531109#post1531109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that there were a few places where vampires could shape change into cows was part of the mythology, I am now visualizing an undead blood drinking bovine on a rampage and still failing to intimidate anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>People don't realize how big cattle can be. On that note, it might be beyond vampiric shapeshifting at Protean 4 to turn into something so large, since wolves and jaguars typically fall far short of 500 to 1000 kg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T12:15:27-08:00","id":1531133,"title":"","content":"Just to clarify I'm not looking for options to change into other shapes than Wolfs and Bats (because that's allready covered by the rules) I looking for option to learn more than two shapes, so that you can have besides wolf and bat, maybe a shape that can swim (like the shark of the Mariner Gangrels) or some small ground based animal like a rat or maybe a cat for scouting in places where a bat wouldn't be that suitable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T12:40:27-08:00","id":1531134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530784-v20-dav20-and-earlier-additional-protean-4-shapes?p=1531133#post1531133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to clarify I'm not looking for options to change into other shapes than Wolfs and Bats (because that's allready covered by the rules) I looking for option to learn more than two shapes, so that you can have besides wolf and bat, maybe a shape that can swim (like the shark of the Mariner Gangrels) or some small ground based animal like a rat or maybe a cat for scouting in places where a bat wouldn't be that suitable.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the text in VDA20, \u0130 think you can only have a fight and a flight form in that edition, unless you make more through advanced powers or combined disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T13:25:42-08:00","id":1531140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530784-v20-dav20-and-earlier-additional-protean-4-shapes?p=1531124#post1531124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People don't realize how big cattle can be. On that note, it might be beyond vampiric shapeshifting at Protean 4 to turn into something so large, since wolves and jaguars typically fall far short of 500 to 1000 kg.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, though a lot of people only think of the modern breeds which are oversized or bred for certain traits which allow for overdevelopment of muscle tissue. There are several breeds that are far smaller than 500 kg and don't even come up to your shoulder.<br /> <br /> Perhaps I am just weird envisioning a micro scottish highland cow stomping around like a belligerent tribble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T20:44:46-08:00","id":1531172,"title":"","content":"I have now noted down the Killer Rabbit of Caerbannog (<i>Monty Python and the Holy Grail</i>) as an idea for future Gangrel characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-20T21:04:48-08:00","id":1531221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530784-v20-dav20-and-earlier-additional-protean-4-shapes?p=1531172#post1531172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have now noted down the Killer Rabbit of Caerbannog (<i>Monty Python and the Holy Grail</i>) as an idea for future Gangrel characters.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://youtu.be/-eQdh6DW0N8?t=61\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Oh, it's just a harmless little bunny, isn't it?&quot; </a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}